      "status": "draft",
      "stem": "In the extraction of copper from its sulphide ore, the metal is finally obtained by the reduction of cuprous oxide with:",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "content": "Copper(I) sulphide",
          "is_correct": true
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "content": "Iron(II) sulphide",
          "is_correct": false
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "content": "Carbon monoxide",
          "is_correct": false
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "content": "Sulfur dioxide",
          "is_correct": false
        }
      ],
      "solution": "Copper is obtained by auto-reduction (self-reduction) where cuprous oxide ($\\mathrm{Cu_2O}$) reacts with remaining cuprous sulphide ($\\mathrm{Cu_2S}$): \n$2\\mathrm{Cu_2O} + \\mathrm{Cu_2S} \\rightarrow 6\\mathrm{Cu} + \\mathrm{SO_2}$."
    },
    {
      "ref": "CHEM-MET-002",
      "subtopic": "extraction-processes",
      "type": "single_correct",
      "difficulty": 3,
      "expected_time_sec": 70,
      "source_type": "pyq",
      "exam": "jee_main",
      "year": 2022,
      "shift": "25 Jul 2022, Shift 1",
      "status": "draft",
      "stem": "In the metallurgy of copper, the slag formed during smelting in the blast furnace is:",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "content": "$\\mathrm{FeSiO_3}$",
          "is_correct": true
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "content": "$\\mathrm{CaSiO_3}$",
          "is_correct": false
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "content": "$\\mathrm{CuSiO_3}$",
          "is_correct": false
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "content": "$\\mathrm{MgSiO_3}$",
          "is_correct": false
        }
      ],
      "solution": "In the extraction of copper, $\\mathrm{FeO}$ is present as an impurity. Silica ($\\mathrm{SiO_2}$) is added as a flux, reacting with iron oxide to form iron silicate slag: $\\mathrm{FeO} + \\mathrm{SiO_2} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{FeSiO_3}$ (slag)."
    }
